 "grid_note": "HOW THE CELLS WERE LOCATED. The 39 vertical rules were detected on the PRINTED HEADING band of this sheet as thin-line maxima of a high-passed darkness profile and then fitted as a single pitch, x = 569.7 + 79.34 n. THE FIRST FIT WAS WRONG AND THE HEADING CAUGHT IT: a template anchored on the strongest 39 detections started one whole column too far right, which put 'Under 5' outside the table and every mark one age band too old. Rendered over the printed heading it was plainly off, and the corrected template reads column 1 'Under 5' under MALES, column 13 '100 and upwards', column 14 'Under 5' under FEMALES and column 26 '100 and upwards'. That check is not optional on this book. The template was then correlated against each row band's own darkness profile to carry the leaning rules, and the 31 writing lines fitted as y = 650 + 75.33 n for the mark band off the names-column ink. Columns 6, 19 and 20 were read a second time as montages of their own 31 cells. This hand writes long horizontal flourishes off the ends of the names, and several of them cross the rule into columns 1 and 2; the footings (column 1 blank, column 2 = 1) are what separate those tails from tallies, and they are recorded as tails, not marks. No cell value here is an OCR output.",
 "cells_state": "partial",
 "cells_note": "Thirty-seven of the thirty-eight columns balance against the figures the enumerator footed on this sheet, including the twenty-two that are blank down the page and blank in the footing and are treated as balanced at zero. ONE DOES NOT: free white females 30 under 40 (column 19) reads 17 against a printed 19, and the column was montaged and re-read and did not move. It is left standing rather than forced: `cells` omits column 19 and `cells_first_pass` carries the whole reading. It is NOT reconciled data and nothing downstream may treat it as such. THE SHAPE OF THIS SHEET IS ITS OWN FINDING: 31 households of which the great majority are a single man in one age band - column 6 and column 7 between them carry 49 of the 116 free white persons on the page - and only three households (lines 25, 27 and 29) carry more than four people. The FREE COLORED block is filled on exactly one line, line 29 (John Johnson): two males 10 under 24, one male 24 under 36, one male 36 under 55 and two females 24 under 36, all four columns footed and balanced. Line 5 carries a seventh free coloured person, one male 36 under 55.",
 "cells_columns_committed": 37,
